# HANDOFF.md — VAYUNX Chat Application (Grade A)

**Last updated**: 2026-07-22 (Phase 5b complete — username discovery + user directory, FR-052/FR-053, all gates green; infra note: app uses native PostgreSQL 18 on :5432, which shadows the Docker postgres container — see §5)

Read this first if you're picking up this project in a new session. It tells you what exists, why, how to run it, and exactly what's next.

---

## 1. What this project is

VAYUNX is a production-quality, end-to-end encrypted chat application. This folder (`Grade_A`) is the **first of several independent "Grade" folders** that will eventually be duplicated with only the cryptographic implementation swapped. Business features, API contracts, database schema, frontend, and project structure are meant to stay identical across grades — **only the crypto implementation differs** (see `CONSTITUTION.md` Principle X).

Grade A's concrete algorithms: Argon2id (passwords), Ed25519 (JWT signing), ML-DSA-65 (identity keys), ML-KEM-768 (key exchange), HKDF-SHA3-256 (KDF), ChaCha20-Poly1305 (message/file encryption), SHA3-256 (hashing), TLS 1.3 hybrid X25519+ML-KEM-768 (transport). Full rationale in `DECISIONS.md`.

## 2. The governing process (read this before doing anything)

The user is running a strict **23-phase, phase-gated development process** (Phase 0 Requirements Analysis → Phase 23 Project Completion), with an explicit approval gate between every phase — nothing proceeds without the user's go-ahead. This is documented in full in the original project brief (see conversation history / `CONSTITUTION.md` Principle IX).

**Critically**: this 23-phase process was implemented via **Spec Kit** (GitHub's spec-driven development toolkit, installed as Claude Code skills under `.claude/skills/speckit-*`), but the full `/speckit-specify` → `/speckit-plan` → `/speckit-tasks` chain was run **once**, covering the entire application (all 11 user stories, all 51 functional requirements). It is **not** re-run per phase. The single `tasks.md` (140 tasks) is the master implementation backlog for the whole app, mapped onto the user's 23 phases as a documented correspondence (see `docs/phases/phase-02-project-structure-report.md`'s intro, or re-derive from `specs/001-e2ee-chat-platform/tasks.md`'s phase structure).

**Going forward, the workflow per phase is**:
1. Implement that phase's tasks from `tasks.md` (models → repositories → services → routers, per story).
2. Actually write and run tests (unit/API/security/crypto-validation as applicable) — never claim "done" without real pass/fail output.
3. Run `ruff`, `mypy --strict`, `bandit` — all must be clean.
4. Write a phase report to `docs/phases/phase-NN-<name>-report.md` (Objectives, What Was Built, Testing Report, Decision Log, Risk Report, Known Limitations, Future Recommendations).
5. **Stop and wait for explicit user approval** before starting the next phase.

No new Spec Kit commands are needed for this loop — only continued implementation. `/speckit-analyze` (read-only, no file writes) can optionally be re-run at any checkpoint as a consistency sanity-check between `spec.md`/`plan.md`/`tasks.md` and what's actually been built; it has been run twice so far and both times found only MEDIUM/LOW issues, all since fixed.

