### Backend (`backend/src/`)

```
api/v1/            # auth.py (register[username]/verify-email/login/logout, rate-limited)
                    # users.py (publish/rotate identity keys, public-key directory,
                    #   /users/me profile, /users/search username resolution, /users/{id} summary)
                    # conversations.py (create/list direct conversations)
                    # messages.py (send/list ciphertext messages, cursor pagination)
api/ws/             # connection_manager.py (Redis pub/sub WebSocket fan-out)
                    # realtime.py (/api/v1/ws — auth-at-upgrade, message.send→message.new)
core/               # config.py, database.py (commit-on-success + session_scope),
                     # error_handling.py, redis_client.py, rate_limit.py, dependencies.py
                     # (auth + messaging DI composition root + get_current_session)
crypto/              # interfaces.py (7 abstractions) + providers/ (Grade-A concrete
                     # implementations) + factory.py (the ONE file a future grade swaps)
models/             # user.py (now with unique indexed `username`), role.py, session.py,
                     # email_verification_token.py, identity_key.py, conversation.py, message.py (US2)
repositories/       # base.py, user/session/token/identity_key/conversation/message
                     # repositories (US2 repos add cursor pagination + rotation;
                     #   user_repo adds get_by_username/username_exists/search_by_username)
schemas/            # base.py, auth.py (RegisterRequest.username + username_taken),
                     # user.py (UserProfileResponse/UserSummaryResponse — no email in summary),
                     # messaging.py (identity keys, conversations, opaque MessageEnvelope, send/list DTOs)
services/            # auth_service.py (register takes username), session_service.py, access_tokens.py,
                     # password_policy.py, errors.py (UsernameAlreadyRegisteredError), audit.py (T047 stub),
                     # email_service.py (arq enqueue),
                     # user_service.py (profile/summary/username search), user_errors.py (UserNotFoundError),
                     # messaging_errors.py, identity_key_service.py (rotation w/
                     #   attestation verify), conversation_service.py (participant
                     #   authz), messaging_service.py (opaque send/list)
workers/            # worker_settings.py (registers send_verification_email), email_jobs.py
main.py             # FastAPI app, CORS, AuthError + MessagingError handlers, rate
                     # limiter, auth + users + conversations + messages + realtime routers
```

Tests mirror this under `backend/tests/{unit,api,security,crypto,performance}/`.

### Frontend (`frontend/src/`)

```
crypto/interfaces.ts           # Mirrors backend crypto interfaces — client-side E2EE boundary
crypto/providers/               # @noble/post-quantum (ML-DSA-65/ML-KEM-768),
                                # @noble/ciphers (ChaCha20-Poly1305), @noble/hashes (HKDF/SHA3)
crypto/bytes.ts                 # base64 + concatBytes helpers (wire format for ciphertext/keys/sigs)
crypto/vault.ts                 # LocalIdentity (ML-DSA-65 + ML-KEM-768 keypairs), localStorage persistence,
                                #   ensureLocalIdentity (idempotent publish of public halves)
crypto/conversationCrypto.ts    # THE E2EE CORE: establishOutbound/Inbound (ML-KEM-768 + HKDF-SHA3-256),
                                #   sealMessage/openMessage (ChaCha20-Poly1305 + ML-DSA-65 sign/verify),
                                #   prepareOutgoing/openIncoming, per-conversation key store
services/apiClient.ts          # REST + WebSocket client (ciphertext+envelope only, never plaintext)
                               # + structured ApiError carrying the backend error_code
services/authService.ts         # register [username] / verifyEmail / login / logout over /api/v1/auth/*
services/userService.ts         # fetchProfile / getUserSummary / searchUsers over /api/v1/users/* (FR-053)
services/messagingService.ts   # publishIdentityKey/rotate/list, conversations, send/listMessages
services/realtimeClient.ts      # WebSocket /api/v1/ws client (auth-at-upgrade, bounded reconnect)
store/authStore.ts              # zustand+persist session store (access token mirrored to apiClient;
                                #   loadProfile() pulls /users/me to fill the authoritative username)
store/messagingStore.ts         # zustand messaging store: identity, conversations, per-conv message logs,
                                #   sendOutgoing (encrypt+POST), ingestRealtimeMessage (decrypt in-browser);
                                #   startConversation(username) resolves via /users/search → createConversation
                                #   (no session copying); peer-username cache for rail/thread labels;
                                #   plaintext kept only in an in-memory side-cache, never persisted (FR-051)
hooks/useRealtime.ts            # connects RealtimeClient for session lifetime, wires message.new→store
types/auth.ts                   # Auth DTOs (username on Register/Auth) + closed AuthErrorCode set + guidance
types/user.ts                   # UserProfileResponse / UserSummaryResponse (FR-053; summary has no email)
types/messaging.ts              # US2 DTOs (envelope, identity keys, conversations, messages, WS events)
components/LatticeField.tsx     # signature: animated ML-KEM key-handshake over a lattice grid
components/AuthShell.tsx        # two-pane auth surface (thesis panel + form)
components/Button.tsx, FormField.tsx, RequireAuth.tsx
pages/Register.tsx, Login.tsx, VerifyEmail.tsx, Conversations.tsx  # Register = Email/Username/Password;
                                #   Conversations = US2 messaging surface (start-by-username, account chip
                                #   + rail/thread show usernames)
styles/global.css               # "cryptographic blueprint" design-token system (+ .conv__* messaging styles)
main.tsx, App.tsx               # React 18 + react-router v6 (lazy routes, RequireAuth guard; / = Conversations)
vite.config.ts                  # dev proxy /api + /ws -> backend :8000
vite-env.d.ts                   # vite/client types for import.meta.env
```

Design system (loaded via the `frontend-design` skill): a "cryptographic blueprint"
identity — cool blueprint-paper surface, deep navy ink, a single vermilion
accent, and the lattice grid (ML-KEM-768 / ML-DSA-65's underlying structure) as
the signature element. Three typefaces: Space Grotesk (display), Spline Sans
(body), JetBrains Mono (fingerprints/data). Reduced-motion respected.

## 4. The single most important architectural fact

**Encryption/decryption of message and file content happens exclusively in the browser, never on the backend.** This is spec `FR-051`, not an implementation detail — the backend only ever stores/relays ciphertext + public envelope metadata (algorithm tag, nonce, ephemeral public keys). If you're ever tempted to add a "decrypt on the server" code path, stop — that violates the spec's core guarantee and `SC-002`.

The backend's own `crypto/` module exists for what legitimately belongs server-side: password hashing (Argon2id), JWT signing (Ed25519), and reference implementations of the message/file ciphers used only for crypto validation test vectors — never invoked against real user plaintext by business logic.

## 5. How to run it right now

```powershell
# Backend (from backend/, requires .env at repo root — already generated for local dev)
cd backend
uvicorn src.main:app --reload
# GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/healthz -> {"status":"ok"}  (only endpoint that exists so far)

# Backend tests (requires Postgres + Redis containers up — see below)
./.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest -q          # 87 passed (59 auth + 10 US2 messaging + 18 username/directory)
./.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m ruff check src alembic tests
./.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m mypy --strict src
./.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m bandit -r src -q
./.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m black --check src alembic tests

# Frontend (dev server proxies /api and /ws to the backend on :8000)
cd frontend
npm run dev      # http://localhost:5173 — Register (Email/Username/Password) / Login / Verify-email / Conversations live
npm test         # 41 passed (apiClient + authService + authStore + Register + messagingService + conversationCrypto + userService + messagingStore)
npm run lint     # eslint clean
npm run build    # tsc -b && vite build — typecheck + production bundle (93 modules)

# Full stack via Docker (Postgres/Redis/MinIO/backend/worker/frontend/TLS proxy)
docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml --env-file .env up -d
```

**Current infrastructure state**: ⚠️ Read this carefully — there is a **native PostgreSQL 18** installed on the host (`C:\Program Files\PostgreSQL\18`) that listens on `127.0.0.1:5432` and **shadows the Docker `postgres` container**. Because `.env`'s `DATABASE_URL` uses `localhost:5432`, the **backend connects to the native PostgreSQL 18, NOT the Docker container** — all migrations (`0001`, `0002`, `0003_username_baseline`) and data live on the native instance. The Docker `docker-postgres-1` container is mapped to the same port but is unused by the app (its port proxy loses to the native service on `127.0.0.1`). pgAdmin / psql from `C:\Program Files\PostgreSQL\18\` also connect to the native instance.

**Credential sync rule**: the database user the app uses is `vayunx` (db `vayunx`), and its password must match `.env`'s `POSTGRES_PASSWORD` + the password embedded in `DATABASE_URL` (currently `Admin@123`, URL-encoded `Admin%40123`). If you change the `vayunx` password inside PostgreSQL (e.g. via pgAdmin), you MUST also update `.env` — or reset the DB user back to `Admin@123`:
```sql
-- run in pgAdmin / native psql, connected to the native PostgreSQL 18 as a superuser:
ALTER USER vayunx WITH PASSWORD 'Admin@123';
```
Editing `POSTGRES_PASSWORD` in `.env` alone does NOT change the running DB's password (it is set once at the DB's init). To change the app's DB password intentionally: `ALTER USER vayunx WITH PASSWORD '<new>';` on the native instance AND update both `POSTGRES_PASSWORD` and `DATABASE_URL` in `.env` (URL-encode special chars: `@`→`%40`).

The `redis` container (`docker-redis-1`) is up — required for rate-limiting + WebSocket pub/sub fan-out tests (no native Redis shadowing). The `mailhog` container (`docker-mailhog-1`) is up (SMTP `:1025`, web inbox `:8025`) — verification emails deliver locally. MinIO has not been started yet (not needed until US4/file sharing). To (re)start the Docker infra: `docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml --env-file .env up -d postgres redis mailhog` (note: the `postgres` service here is shadowed by the native PG18 — see above).

